-- functions.spl — LLM function definitions for Recipe 89: arXiv Digest (EAAI-27 workshop)
-- Imported by summarize_arxiv_paper.spl via IMPORT 'functions.spl'.
--
-- Two-step map-reduce per paper, matching the EAAI-27 workshop capstone spec
-- (docs/conference/EAAI-2027/.../handout.md, "Capstone Demo: arXiv Paper
-- Summarization"): one summary per section (map), then one structured
-- per-paper digest — a paragraph per section plus a 3-bullet contribution
-- summary (reduce).

CREATE FUNCTION section_summarizer(section_title TEXT, section_text TEXT, max_tokens INT)
RETURNS TEXT
AS $$
You are a technical summarizer. Produce a concise summary of the following
research paper section in plain English. Focus on methods and findings.
Stay well under {max_tokens} words — leave headroom, since generation is cut
off at a hard token limit and an unfinished sentence is worse than a shorter
complete one. Write 2-4 complete sentences and stop; do not pad toward the
limit. Write plain prose only — no headings, no bullet points, no preamble
such as "This section...".

Section: {section_title}

{section_text}
$$;

CREATE FUNCTION paper_digest_writer(title TEXT, section_summaries TEXT, max_tokens INT)
RETURNS TEXT
AS $$
You are a research editor producing a structured digest of one paper for a
live audience unfamiliar with it. You are given per-section summaries below,
each already condensed. Using ONLY the information in these summaries (do
not invent details not present in them), write:

1. One paragraph per section, in the same order as given, each introduced by
   the section's name as a bold label (e.g. "**Introduction:** ..."). Keep
   each paragraph to at most 5 complete sentences — a paper with many
   sections needs shorter paragraphs than one with few, since every section
   AND the Key Contributions block below must fit in the length budget.
2. A final "**Key Contributions:**" block with exactly 3 bullet points
   capturing the paper's core contribution, method, and main result. This
   block is mandatory — never omit it or leave it unfinished.

Hard length budget: {max_tokens} words total, generation is cut off at a hard
token limit with no warning. Budget your words across ALL sections plus the
Key Contributions block BEFORE writing, so you reach a complete final bullet
rather than running out of room partway through — a shorter digest that
finishes cleanly is far better than a longer one truncated mid-sentence.
Write Markdown.

Paper title: {title}

Section summaries:
{section_summaries}
$$;
